        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "EXAMPLE 2A-19 STRUCTURE MOTION DUE TO AIR SHOCK ",
            "block_bbox": [
                247,
                289,
                937,
                310
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 1
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Required:Maximum horizontal acceleration, velocity and displacement of the square structure shown in Figure 2A-9 (+) from Problem 2A-10 for a surface burst of 5,000 lbs at a distance from the front wall of 155 ft. Assume a coarse and compact soil. Roof, floor slab and side walls are 1 foot thick reinforced concrete slabs and assume a 50 psf of internal dead load for the structure.",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                349,
                1046,
                479
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 2
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Step 1.External loadings on the structure are determined according to the procedure in Example 2A-10. See Figure 2A-10 (+), Figure 2A-12 (+) and Figure 2A-13 (+). The arrival time (tA) for these loads are tabulated in Step 3d of Example 2A-10.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                500,
                1044,
                603
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 3
        },
        {
            "block_label": "formula",
            "block_content": "\\begin{aligned}&t_{Af}\\left(\\mathrm{f}\\mathrm{r}\\mathrm{o}\\mathrm{n}\\mathrm{t}\\mathrm{w}\\mathrm{a}\\mathrm{l}\\right)=60.9\\mathrm{~m}\\mathrm{s}\\\\ &t_{Ab}\\left(\\mathrm{r}\\mathrm{e}\\mathrm{a}\\mathrm{r}\\mathrm{w}\\mathrm{a}\\mathrm{l}\\right)=83.6\\mathrm{~m}\\mathrm{s}\\\\ \\end{aligned}",
            "block_bbox": [
                344,
                624,
                597,
                694
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 4
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Step 2.",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                714,
                212,
                738
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 5
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "a. Calculate area of front and rear walls.",
            "block_bbox": [
                275,
                760,
                701,
                780
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 6
        },
        {
            "block_label": "formula",
            "block_content": "\\mathrm{A}\\mathrm{r}\\mathrm{e}\\mathrm{a}\\left(\\mathrm{f}\\mathrm{r}\\mathrm{o}\\mathrm{n}\\mathrm{d}\\mathrm{r}\\mathrm{e}\\mathrm{a}\\right)=30\\times12\\times\\left(12\\right)^{2}=51840\\mathrm{~in}^{2}",
            "block_bbox": [
                343,
                799,
                866,
                827
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 7
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "b.Calculate the time difference between the rear and front walls from Step 1.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                273,
                847,
                1036,
                897
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 8
        },
        {
            "block_label": "formula",
            "block_content": "\\delta t=t_{Ab}-t_{Af}=83.6-60.9=22.7ms ",
            "block_bbox": [
                344,
                920,
                713,
                942
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 9
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "C.Construct the horizontal force-time load curve by multiplying the values of the front and rear wall curves from Step 1 by the area from Step 2a. Rear wall load starts at time equal to .$\\delta t=22.7$ from Step 2b. See Figure 2A-26 (+).\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                274,
                964,
                1025,
                1071
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 10
        },
        {
